  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Local Humanitarian Leadership</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of this investment is to strengthen the ASAL Humanitarian Network (AHN) Secretariat to increase strategic leadership in building its own capacity, setting its governance structures, and strategy. These will include among the many - i. Training the Chief Executive Officers (CEOs) of the AHN member organisations on governance and leadership of network. ii. Avail funds to the trained Secretariat to invest in key urgent areas of their choice emerging from the training that can help move the AHN to the next level of leadership, including development of an overall strategy, fundraising strategy, etc. Mapping of Arid and Semi -Arid Land (ASAL) partners, against location, competency, capacity, donors, International Non governmental Organisation (INGO) partners self -assessment of an organisations own capacities will enable the prioritisation of areas where organisations want to focus on [SHAPE?] Mapping of specialist service providers offers (i.e. INGOs or other Local Non Governmental Organisations (LNGOS), recognised consultants).  Additional funds will support  1.Gender equality  promotion through influencing gender policy design and implementation 2.Strengthened referral pathways and community based GBV response and prevention. 3.Strengthened leadership, visibility and effectiveness of AHN&apos;s Women Rights Organizations to deliver gender strategy . The project also has some additional 2year funding from Oxfam Denmark -IBIS. Through these funds, PGI in Garissa and MWADO in Marsabit will support crisis affected communities by providing cash grants through the Survivor and Community -Led Response (SCLR) approach. The SCLR approach recognizes that crisis -affected people are the first and last responders in any disaster and allows humanitarian aid to better strengthen the communal resilience of affected people. It uses microgrants to transfer power and resources to existing and emergent community self -help groups and organisations that mobilise during every crisis, all</narrative>
  </description>
